files:

;_NAME.tsv - trial files to dsownload data

8_trm5.tsv - data found with https://alphaknot.cent.uw.edu.pl/browse/?field=gene_name&val=trm5%25&conj=AND&field=Category&val=AF4&raw=1&result_cols=Knot_type;Category;Uniprot;Organism;pLDDT_knotcore;Protein_name;InterPro;Gene_name;
    gene_name = trm5* - mostly trm56; category = af4

38tys_trmd.tsv - data found with https://alphaknot.cent.uw.edu.pl/browse/?field=InterPro&val=IPR002649;IPR016009;IPR019230;IPR023148;IPR029026;IPR029028&conj=NOT&field=Category&val=ESM1&raw=1&result_cols=Category;Uniprot;Organism;Gene_name;InterPro;Protein_name
    by interpro values; not esm1

38tys-_trmd.tsv - https://alphaknot.cent.uw.edu.pl/browse/?field=InterPro&val=IPR002649;IPR016009;IPR019230;IPR023148;IPR029026;IPR029028&conj=AND&field=Category&val=AF4&raw=1
    by interpro; only AF4 (bo byly duplikaty z af1-knot)

web_ak_data_trmD.tsv - to jest bezposrednie raw data z strony alphaknota wraz z wybraniem wszystkich typow AF 

450_nep1.tsv - https://alphaknot.cent.uw.edu.pl/browse/?field=Protein_name&val=NEP1%25&conj=AND&field=Category&val=AF4&raw=1&result_cols=Knot_type;Category;Uniprot;Organism;pLDDT_knotcore;Protein_name;InterPro;Gene_name;
    Protein_name = nep1%25; cat=af4

880_nep1.tsv - https://alphaknot.cent.uw.edu.pl/browse/?field=Gene_name&val=nep1%25&conj=NOT&field=Category&val=ESM1&raw=1&result_cols=Category;Uniprot;Organism;Gene_name;InterPro;Protein_name
    gene_name = nep1%25; not esm1

matched_i _intAct.tsv - those are the alphaknot data that was found in intact using uniprot ids

alphaknot_data_from_1.tsv / alphaknot_data_from_2.tsv - files from find_duplicates.py; contain alphanot data of the unique uniprot ids from the 38tys_trmd.tsv and web_ak_data_trmD.tsv accordingly


unique_in_1.tsv /unique_in_2.tsv - files from find_duplicates.py; contain the uniprot ids from the 38tys_trmd.tsv and web_ak_data_trmD.tsv accordingly
scripts:

.py:
api.py - download api of alphaknot usining interpro ids

count_interactions.py - sums up the number of interpro ids in the files

find_duplicates.py - i had differences in the numebr of web searches of trmd and the one that i got from api, so i wanted to check which where unique for each and find out what the proteins were

check_if_in_inact.py: checks for uniprot ids in a file that are in the database (ecoli as of now) of intact